{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1145860-sex-ratio-in-corax-ratkin-and-camazotz","id":1145860,"title":"Sex Ratio in Corax, Ratkin and Camazotz","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-01T11:54:35-07:00","id":1145860,"title":"Sex Ratio in Corax, Ratkin and Camazotz","content":"SO it popped in my head today while preparing for my game next week...would there be a sex ratio offset in the Corax, Ratkin and Camazotz who come from cultures where there is a strong preference for males over females for example. Since these breeds have to perform a rite to make their children full shifters instead of luck at birth...they could in theory mess with how even their population is. Thoughts? Or do you think Gaian culture and their totems would step in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 10-01-2017, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T16:35:53-07:00","id":1145911,"title":"","content":"First and foremost, those come from eclectic and chaotic Fera cultures that don't share the same outlook. If a kid looks like they might do well with a spirit egg or passing the plague, and there's someone around to initiate anointment of this precious gift, then everything is go. This is particularly true of Ratkin, since their greatest desire in modern times is to wreck all of humanity's shit and they sometimes take up banners of anyone pushed down into the dirt and grime to accomplish this end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T17:14:40-07:00","id":1145918,"title":"","content":"For Ratkin I can see being able to study someone and make a choice based on their personality and life and how well they'd contribute. But the Camazotz and Corax have to enact the rite while the initiate is an infant. How would they be able to make a guess at that age? I'm not arguing that we need pockets of sexist Ravens and Bats, so much as I'm curious about this. I want to make sure I&quot;m not viewing my groups through rose colored glasses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T18:27:26-07:00","id":1145932,"title":"","content":"Homid culture affects garou culture, so I don't see why the changing breeds would be any different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15478-celinikal","name":"celinikal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T22:51:17-07:00","id":1145985,"title":"","content":"Most people who get the birthing plague die, I mean Rodens so outnumber the Homid Ratkin they basically have no say in how the breed functions. Similarly Corax can't pick the same breed for their rites. A Homid corax has to pick a random bird's egg and a Corvus Corax has to pick a human I imagine this leads to some signficant variation from human culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T02:02:59-07:00","id":1146001,"title":"","content":"Unless you're playing a 1500 campaign I wouldn't worry about Camazotz since they're quite extinct =P<br /> Ratkin and Corax are from all over the world now, especially the rats.... while there could be in some culture the idea of &quot;having a male descendent&quot; those cultures surely aren't too invasive in the modern era.<br /> <br /> Also, I may be wrong but it's not like Ratkins reproduce through rituals like the Corax... they procreate like every other fera, with the extra chance to bite a kinfolk and attempt to induce a first change. Being that the bite is potentially lethal though I doubt that many Ratkins would choose to elevate that favourite kinfolk son they're planning to leave everything to, since the chances of not having a favourite son anymore are quite high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T08:15:21-07:00","id":1146064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1145860-sex-ratio-in-corax-ratkin-and-camazotz?p=1146001#post1146001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're playing a 1500 campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol Actually......its why the thought came to my head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T08:35:57-07:00","id":1146067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1145860-sex-ratio-in-corax-ratkin-and-camazotz?p=1146064#post1146064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol Actually......its why the thought came to my head</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh =P<br /> In that case I'd say that yes, both Corax and Camazotz are going to have a sensible difference in numbers between males and females, but I think the Ratkin would still be quite balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}